Original Question:

 I need to run an UPS script automatically when tru64 boots up. I=20
> know I need to modify the following script with an option of start=20
> and stop and I have to copy these files in /sbin/initd. I tried but=20
> it's not happening. I will be happy if gurus can help me to modify=20
> the following script and procedure for automatic startup. We are=20
> using Tru64 version 5.1a .
>=20
>=20




Answer:

After moving the script to the /sbin/init.d directory, you have to link
it to the /sbin/rc3.d directory.

#  cd  /sbin/rc3.d
#  ln  -s  ../init.d/<scriptname> S99<scriptname>


I also found a script which can automate the above activity. Example of =
that script is as follows:


#!/sbin/sh
#

PATH=3D/sbin:/bin:/usr/bin:/etc:/usr/sbin:/usr/ucb
export PATH
script=3D/sbin/init.d/powerflag
killscript=3D/sbin/rc0.d/K00powerflag
startscript=3D/sbin/rc3.d/S60powerflag
#
if [ ! -x $script ]; then
  cp pf_boot.osf1 $script
  chmod 744 $script
fi
#
if [ ! -x $startscript ]; then
  ln $script $startscript
  chmod 744 $startscript
fi
#
if [ ! -x $killscript ]; then
  ln $script $killscript
  chmod 744 $killscript
fi


